course: dictionary
lesson: 15731
title: Transformed: changed completely
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: When something is transformed, it is changed so much that it looks, acts or is a different kind of thing. «The caterpillar was transformed into a butterfly.» The caterpillar did not just grow bigger. Its whole body changed, so transformed means changed completely.
explain: Look at the words around it for clues. «The old shed was transformed into a cosy reading den.» The shed was not just given a fresh coat of paint. It became something new, so transformed means changed completely, and here the change is a good one.
explain: Transformed can also describe a person. «After weeks at the animal shelter, Sam was a transformed boy: he smiled, he shared, and he was brave.» Sam changed inside, not only in looks. Try swapping in changed: the sentence still makes sense.
fact: Transform means change completely in shape, look or nature.
fact: «Transformed» is the past form of «transform», so «transformed into» shows something has become something else.
fact: «Transformed by» tells you what caused the change, as in «transformed by kindness».
fact: In maths, a transformed shape has been moved, flipped, turned or resized.
fact: In science, a caterpillar is transformed into a butterfly, and in stories a character can be transformed by kindness.
exercise: «The caterpillar was transformed into a butterfly.» What does transformed mean here? | Painted in bright colours | Found and picked up | *Changed completely | Moved a little to one side
exercise: «The old barn was transformed into a theatre.» Find and copy the word that shows the barn has changed completely. | old | *transformed | theatre | barn
exercise: In maths, a shape that has been flipped, turned or resized has been what? | Counted | Forgotten | Rounded | *Transformed
test: «The team was transformed by hard training.» What does transformed suggest? | Made to sleep | Painted over | Sent home early | *Changed a lot, usually for the better
test: Tomas says transformed only means moved. Is he right? | Yes, it only means painted | *No, it can mean changed completely, and in maths it can mean moved, flipped, turned or resized | No, it means lost | Yes, it only means moved
exam: «The tadpole was ____ into a frog.» Choose the word that fits best. | hidden | *transformed | slept | pulled
